X-Harness-Test-Only: commit=c5f5335aea103a44f5055640aab1375ebca03c39 parent=9c2ac4f3094260e028c46aa1f06b2ccc5533868c tree=d9727693b6920e9c0946c305248b1c96366f5ebb
Subject: [PATCH] test(core): a wait that is sent again is not a loop

Test files only: the failing tests of the fork patch that stops the loop
guard from counting the repeats of a tool call that blocked for a long
time (a bounded wait on a background job, sent again while the job runs).

loop-detection.test.ts (new): the exemption read from HAMH_WAIT_S and
HAMH_WAIT_CAP_S, the threshold of half of the bound, at most 50 seconds
and at least 5 seconds, quick identical calls counted as before, the
repeats of a call that blocked at least the threshold not counted and not
warned about, the waits that sessions send under the harness's bounds,
the cap of the exempt time, a new run of identical calls after another
call, no exemption without the harness's bound, and reset.
session-runtime-orchestrator.test.ts: six identical waits of 240 s and of
100 s with a bound of 240 s do not stop the run; the same calls returning
at once or after 49 s do, and so do the waits without the bound.
